Package: gotochanger
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, adduser
Description: Fake SCSI tape autochanger simulator for testing backup software
 gotochanger simulates a tape autochanger (virtual library) for staging and
 development environments, similar to what a real Dell ML3 or comparable
 tape library provides, but backed entirely by regular files:
 .
  * Storage slots, Import/Export (I/O / "mail slot") elements and multiple
    virtual drives, modeled after the SCSI Medium Changer (SMC) element
    types.
  * A REST API covering every action (load, unload, move, import, export,
    eject, volume creation/deletion, drive fault injection, token
    management).
  * An embedded web management UI to inspect and operate the library
    (move cartridges, insert/eject media) without a CLI.
  * A drop-in replacement for Bareos's disk-changer.in "Changer Command"
    script (gotochanger-changer), plus a general admin CLI
    (gotochangerctl).
 .
  * SNMPv2c trap notifications on library events (load/unload/move/
    import/eject/drive fault/volume full), for testing NMS integrations.
 .
 This package does not create real kernel SCSI devices; it is a userspace
 simulation intended for testing backup software configuration, alerting
 and automation against a realistic virtual autochanger. See the
 gotochanger-kernel package for an optional add-on that does expose real
 kernel SCSI devices.

Package: gotochanger-kernel
Architecture: any
Depends: gotochanger (= ${binary:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, polkitd
Description: Real kernel SCSI devices (TCMU/LIO) for gotochanger
 Optional add-on for gotochanger that exposes real kernel SCSI medium-
 changer and tape-drive devices (/dev/sg*) via the kernel's TCMU/LIO
 (target_core_user) subsystem, instead of the base package's plain-file/
 symlink "Changer Command Script" mode - so backup software sees an
 actual SCSI autochanger and tape drives, not a userspace script
 convention.
 .
 Ships gotochanger-tcmud and a templated gotochanger-tcmud@.service
 systemd unit (one instance per logical library, or @default for the
 whole physical library) - not started or enabled automatically on
 install, since it requires the target_core_user kernel module and root.
 .
 Requires the target_core_user kernel module (loaded automatically at
 boot via a shipped modules-load.d entry once this package is installed;
 a running system may need `modprobe target_core_user` or a reboot
 before that takes effect) and must run as root, unlike the base
 gotochanger service.
